The regional audit shows why the current mesh still cannot pass: rigid island interiors are excellent (all five max at ~1.00035×), but 2,709 welded edges join different rigid islands and 12,067 welded edges join rigid plate directly to cloth; those boundary sets reach 121–218× at p99. Even cloth-only p99 is still 1.88–2.85×.

I’m applying the binding-level repair that preserves the fused mesh: a 40 mm heat-weighted transition band around metallic/non-metallic and articulated plate boundaries, with only the eroded plate cores collapsed rigidly, plus graph smoothing of heat weights before the top-four limit. This uses the brief’s prescribed joint blend width and keeps each retained plate core rigid while giving welded boundary triangles compatible weights.
